# Local CI verification evidence.
#
# Transient by design. artifacts/local-ci/latest.json describes one run on one machine; committing
# it would put a claim about a past verification into the repository, where a later reader could
# mistake it for a statement about the current commit. The durable record of a verified commit is
# the evidence block scripts/submit-pr.mjs writes into the pull request, which is attached to the
# SHA it actually names.
#
# This is also what keeps CI from dirtying the working tree: scripts/submit-pr.mjs refuses to run
# against a dirty tree, and the pipeline writes here.
artifacts/local-ci/

# This repository has no dependencies and no install step. node_modules should never exist; the
# dependency-freedom stage in scripts/ci-pipeline.mjs fails if it does. Ignored so that an
# accidental `npm install` during debugging cannot be committed on top of that failure.
node_modules/
